# Search-tool ignore list (ripgrep, fd, and anything else honouring `.ignore`).
#
# Why this file exists: the repository root holds several GENERATED or
# DUPLICATE-CHECKOUT trees. A recursive text search started at the root walks
# into them and reads the same source many times over — most visibly
# `.claude/worktrees/`, which holds a full additional checkout per parallel
# helper. This file makes the common agent/developer search tools skip them by
# default, so an unscoped search still lands on the tracked source tree.
#
# This is a convenience layer, not a boundary:
#   * `git grep` (the recommended way to search this repo) ignores this file
#     entirely and always searches exactly the tracked tree.
#   * `rg --no-ignore` / `rg -uu` searches these paths anyway when you mean to.
# Unlike `.gitignore`, `.ignore` is still honoured under `rg --no-ignore-vcs`,
# which is why the two lists are kept separately even where they overlap.
#
# Rule for editing: every entry here must be a generated tree or an additional
# checkout — never a directory holding source that is tracked in THIS
# repository. The one gitlink below (`vendor/tor`) is a third-party submodule
# whose contents `git grep` does not descend into either.

# Build output.
build/

# Per-run test scratch.
test-tmp/

# One full additional checkout per parallel helper.
.claude/worktrees/

# Source-navigator index cache.
.codeindex/

# Chaos-harness run artifacts.
chaos-output/

# Third-party dependencies fetched/built by `make vendor`.
vendor/tor/
vendor/zclassic-ref/
vendor/.cache/
vendor/.build/

# Generated artifacts over 200 KB; open them by path. Never list source here.
docs/API_REFERENCE.md
docs/work/retrieval-gold-evidence/*.jsonl
contexts/commons/corpus/evidence-*.json
tools/lint/cyclomatic_complexity_baseline.txt

# Historical documents; open by path. Tracked, kept for evidence only.
docs/archive/
